.TH NNI 8 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
nni \- settings, information and upkeep for YnniOS and SGnniOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nni
.RB [ info ]
.br
.B nni list
.br
.B nni get
.I KEY
.br
.B nni set
.I KEY VALUE
.br
.B nni apply
.RB [ \-\-boot | \-\-x ]
.br
.B nni wallpaper
.RB [ list | \fIN\fP | \fINAME\fP | \fIFILE\fP | next ]
.br
.B nni theme
.RB [ list | \fIN\fP | \fINAME\fP | next | none ]
.br
.B nni update
.br
.B nni version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nni
is the settings tool of the nni family: YnniOS (built on Debian) and
SGnniOS (built on Gentoo).
Every system setting lives in one file,
.IR /etc/nni.conf ,
described in
.BR nni.conf (5).
.B nni set
changes a setting and applies it straight away, so there is no need to
reboot or to remember which program handles which file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR info " (default)"
A short summary: distribution, edition, version and codename, kernel,
hostname, time zone, Wi\-Fi and splash settings, and the services that start
at boot.
.TP
.B list
Every setting with its value and a one\-line explanation.
.TP
.BI get " KEY"
Print one setting.
.TP
.BI set " KEY VALUE"
Check the value, save it in
.I /etc/nni.conf
and apply it now. Key names are not case sensitive. Needs root.
.TP
.B apply
Apply every setting again (hostname, time zone, console keymap and font,
wallpaper). Use it after editing
.I /etc/nni.conf
by hand. Needs root.
.B \-\-boot
is used by the boot script.
.B \-\-x
is run from
.I ~/.xinitrc
before the desktop starts: it applies the keyboard layout, loads the X
resources (nni's defaults, then the theme's colours, then
.IR ~/.Xresources ,
so yours win) and sets the wallpaper. It works for normal users too.
.TP
.BR wallpaper " [" list | \fIN\fP | \fINAME\fP | \fIFILE\fP | next ]
Without an argument, list the installed wallpapers with the current one
marked. With a number or name, switch to it (full edition, package
nni\-artwork);
.B next
takes the one after the current. A full path to any picture works too.
Changing the wallpaper keeps the theme's colours.
.TP
.BR theme " [" list | \fIN\fP | \fINAME\fP | next | none ]
A theme is a wallpaper with colours to match: NiWM's window borders,
nibar's background, text and accent, and the terminal's 16 colours. The
four themes are named after the wallpapers: Debian Crimson, Midnight Blue,
Pastel Sunrise and Amber Dark. Without an argument, list them with the
current one marked. Pick one by number, name (any case, spaces or
dashes) or id; it applies at once. NiWM and nibar change colour straight
away; terminals opened after the change use the new colours.
.B none
leaves the colours to niwmrc, nibarc and
.IR ~/.Xresources .
Also available as
.BR nni\-theme .
.IP
Your own themes go in
.I /etc/nni/themes
as
.IR id .theme
files. Copy one from
.I /usr/share/nni/themes
and change it: each line is
.IB KEY =\(dq value \(dq\fR.\fP
The keys are NAME, WALLPAPER (a number, name or file), ACCENT, BORDER
and URGENT (NiWM's focused, normal and urgent borders), BAR_BG, BAR_FG
and LOGO (nibar's background, text and chicken colour, or auto), TERM_BG
and TERM_FG, and PALETTE, the terminal's 16 colours separated by spaces.
A theme in /etc/nni/themes with the same id replaces ours.
.IP
Themes reach the programs as X resources, so a line in
.I ~/.config/niwm/niwmrc
or
.I ~/.config/niwm/nibarc
that sets a colour itself always wins over the theme.
.TP
.BR update " (also " upgrade )
Upgrade the nni packages themselves: nni\-base (and nni\-artwork when
installed) on YnniOS through
.BR pol (8),
app\-misc/nni\-base on SGnniOS through Portage. On SGnniOS the first run
switches the overlay the ISO shipped with to the one on GitHub.
.TP
.B version
Name, version, codename and edition.
.SH SETTINGS
HOSTNAME, TIMEZONE, KEYMAP, CONSOLE_FONT, XKB_LAYOUT, WIFI_AUTO, WALLPAPER,
THEME and SPLASH. See
.BR nni.conf (5)
for what each one does.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nni set TIMEZONE America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires
nni set HOSTNAME chick\-lab
nni set XKB_LAYOUT latam
nni set WIFI_AUTO yes
nni wallpaper 2
nni theme "Midnight Blue"
nni\-theme next
nni update
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nni.conf
All settings.
.TP
.IR /etc/nni/distro ", " /etc/nni/edition
Which distribution and edition this is.
.TP
.I /usr/share/nni/
Logos, fastfetch layouts, the splash picture, the handbook, VERSION and
CODENAME.
.TP
.I /etc/os\-release
Written by
.BR nni ;
Debian's or Gentoo's own copy is set aside so upgrades keep the name.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when a command or value is not accepted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nni.conf (5),
.BR svc (8),
.BR wifi (8),
.BR pol (8),
.BR spol (8),
.BR handbook (1)
